  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish several relevant but disconnected ideas: elevated-temperature treatment and atomistic simulation of HEAs, temperature-activated lattice diffusion and structural disorder, nanoscale surface-energy-driven reshaping, chemical clustering or short-range order, and selective elemental loss during melting or corrosion. R18 is particularly relevant to surface free energy and diffusion-rich interfaces, while R2 suggests preferential loss of lower-melting constituents during laser processing. However, none describes vacuum heating of multicomponent HEA nanoparticles or predicts that surface-energy differences will drive Au/Cu surface segregation followed by evaporation, coalescence, and spherical reshaping. Thus the literature points in the general direction, but identifying the specific alloy, intervention, and coupled segregation–evaporation mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
